INT. COLD STORAGE WAREHOUSE - NIGHT

Frost on steel racks. Breath fogs. A forklift sits idle.

RAFAEL "RAFA" ZUNIGA (40s, crew chief) crouches beside a pallet of frozen tuna. Earpiece in.

BEATRIX LUND (30s, safecracker) rolls a case across the floor. YUSUF KANDEMIR (20s, driver) leans on the forklift, eating an apple.

RAFA
Thirty minutes. Guard rotation is clockwork.

YUSUF
Always is, until it isn't.

BEATRIX
Relax. Nobody's coming.

Two more shapes move between the racks: OSEI MENSAH (50s, tech) and LIV HARTWELL (30s, inside woman, wearing a warehouse vest). They set a monitor on a pallet.

OSEI
Cameras loop. Thirty seconds of clean footage, then it resets.

LIV
My badge opens the vault door. After that, it's yours.

Everybody breathes easier. Yusuf laughs. Rafa almost smiles.

Then the lights snap on. Full white. A klaxon wails.

DOMINIK VOSS (50s, security director, long coat) steps out from behind a rack with a pistol at his side. Four armed guards fan out behind him.

Rafa, Beatrix, Yusuf, Osei and Liv freeze. Nobody moves.

DOMINIK
Evening, everyone. Liv. Thank you for the invitation.

Liv doesn't look at anyone. Beatrix lunges at her; Osei catches Beatrix by the arm. Yusuf drops the apple and bolts. The guards tackle him against the racks.

RAFA
Liv. What did you do?

LIV
What I had to.

Dominik raises a hand. The klaxon stops. The only sound is Yusuf's ragged breathing and the hum of the freezers.
